  "ai_usage": "Use for any file intake — attachments, avatar/logo upload, CSV import, document submission.\n\nThe one structural rule: the drop zone must wrap a real <input type=\"file\">, hidden with the clip-rect visually-hidden pattern, NOT display:none or visibility:hidden — those remove it from the accessibility tree and the tab order, and you lose keyboard and touch users, who cannot drag anything. Wrapping it in a <label> gives you click-to-open, focus, and Enter/Space activation for free; do not reimplement those with key handlers.\n\nDrag state: dragenter/dragleave fire for every child element, so track a depth counter (++ on enter, -- on leave, active while > 0) instead of toggling a boolean, or the highlight strobes. Call preventDefault in dragover or the drop never fires, and add a window-level dragover/drop guard so a missed drop does not navigate the page to the file.\n\nValidate on both paths: the accept attribute filters the picker but does NOT filter drops, so re-check type and size in your drop handler, and re-check everything server side regardless. Progress here is a timer stub — replace it with xhr.upload.onprogress, or fetch with a streamed body, and handle failure per row rather than failing the whole queue.\n\nAvoid: making drag the only way in, blocking the UI during upload, silently dropping files that exceed a limit (say which file and why), and forgetting to revoke object URLs if you add thumbnails.",
  "path": "effects/forms-inputs/file-dropzone.html",
  "source": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>File Drop Zone</title>\n  <script type=\"application/json\" id=\"effect-meta\">\n  {\n    \"id\": \"file-dropzone\",\n    \"title\": \"File Drop Zone\",\n    \"summary\": \"Drag-and-drop upload area with a dashed target, live drag state, and a queued file list with progress bars.\",\n    \"description\": \"A drop target that is also a real file input, which is the part most implementations get wrong. The dashed frame lifts and tints on dragover, driven by a drag counter so that dragging across a child element does not flicker the state off and on. Dropped or picked files land in a queue with a type icon, a human-readable size, and a progress bar; the label wraps a visually-hidden <input type=\\\"file\\\"> so the whole zone is clickable, focusable, and operable from the keyboard without a single extra listener.\",\n    \"theme\": \"forms-inputs\",\n    \"categories\": [\"form\", \"input\", \"upload\", \"drag-and-drop\"],\n    \"tags\": [\"file-upload\", \"dropzone\", \"drag-and-drop\", \"input\", \"form\", \"progress\", \"queue\", \"dragover\", \"accessibility\"],\n    \"tech\": [\"css\", \"js\", \"html\"],\n    \"era\": \"2020s\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"intermediate\",\n    \"dependencies\": [],\n    \"browser_support\": \"All modern browsers. Drag-and-drop needs a pointer; the wrapped file input is the fallback everywhere else, including touch and keyboard.\",\n    \"performance_notes\": \"Listeners are bound once on the zone plus a window-level guard that stops the browser navigating away when a file is dropped outside it. Rendering is one row per file. Progress here is simulated on a timer — swap it for real XHR/fetch upload events.\",\n    \"accessibility_notes\": \"The zone is a <label> wrapping a visually-hidden (not display:none) file input, so it stays in the tab order, announces as a file control, and opens the picker on Enter or Space with no key handling of our own. Drag state is decorative only — every action is reachable without dragging. The queue is an aria-live=\\\"polite\\\" region so added files are announced once. Focus is shown with a real outline, and the dashed border is not the only cue for the drag state.\",\n    \"customization\": [\n      { \"name\": \"--accent\", \"description\": \"Active/dragover tint and progress fill\", \"default\": \"#7c5cff\" },\n      { \"name\": \"--line\", \"description\": \"Resting dashed border colour\", \"default\": \"#2b3145\" },\n      { \"name\": \"accept\", \"description\": \"Restrict pickable types on the input; validate again on drop, since dropping bypasses accept\", \"default\": \"unset\" },\n      { \"name\": \"MAX_MB\", \"description\": \"Client-side size guard — always re-check server side\", \"default\": \"10\" }\n    ],\n    \"variations\": [\n      \"Paste-to-upload by listening for paste and reading event.clipboardData.files\",\n      \"Image thumbnails via URL.createObjectURL, revoked on removal\",\n      \"Chunked/resumable upload for large files\",\n      \"Restrict to a single file and replace rather than append\"\n    ],\n    \"related\": [\"floating-label-input\", \"password-strength\", \"tag-input\"],\n    \"ai_usage\": \"Use for any file intake — attachments, avatar/logo upload, CSV import, document submission.\\n\\nThe one structural rule: the drop zone must wrap a real <input type=\\\"file\\\">, hidden with the clip-rect visually-hidden pattern, NOT display:none or visibility:hidden — those remove it from the accessibility tree and the tab order, and you lose keyboard and touch users, who cannot drag anything. Wrapping it in a <label> gives you click-to-open, focus, and Enter/Space activation for free; do not reimplement those with key handlers.\\n\\nDrag state: dragenter/dragleave fire for every child element, so track a depth counter (++ on enter, -- on leave, active while > 0) instead of toggling a boolean, or the highlight strobes. Call preventDefault in dragover or the drop never fires, and add a window-level dragover/drop guard so a missed drop does not navigate the page to the file.\\n\\nValidate on both paths: the accept attribute filters the picker but does NOT filter drops, so re-check type and size in your drop handler, and re-check everything server side regardless. Progress here is a timer stub — replace it with xhr.upload.onprogress, or fetch with a streamed body, and handle failure per row rather than failing the whole queue.\\n\\nAvoid: making drag the only way in, blocking the UI during upload, silently dropping files that exceed a limit (say which file and why), and forgetting to revoke object URLs if you add thumbnails.\"\n  }\n  </script>\n  <style>\n    :root {\n      --bg: #0b0d12;\n      --surface: #12151f;\n      --line: #2b3145;\n      --text: #e7ebf3;\n      --muted: #8b93a7;\n      --accent: #7c5cff;\n      --ok: #2dd4bf;\n      --radius: 12px;\n    }\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; }\n    body {\n      background: var(--bg); color: var(--text);\n      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;\n      display: grid; place-content: center; padding: 1rem;\n    }\n    .wrap { width: min(400px, 92vw); }\n\n    /* Visually hidden but still focusable and announced — never display:none. */\n    .sr {\n      position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; margin: -1px;\n      overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); white-space: nowrap; border: 0;\n    }\n\n    .zone {\n      display: grid; place-items: center; gap: .3rem;\n      padding: 1.4rem 1rem; text-align: center; cursor: pointer;\n      background: var(--surface);\n      border: 2px dashed var(--line);\n      border-radius: var(--radius);\n      transition: border-color .18s, background .18s, transform .18s cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1);\n    }\n    .zone:hover { border-color: #3c4460; }\n    .zone.is-over {\n      border-color: var(--accent);\n      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 12%, var(--surface));\n      transform: scale(1.015);\n    }\n    /* Focus lives on the input, so mirror it onto the label. */\n    .zone:has(input:focus-visible) { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 3px; }\n\n    .zone svg { width: 26px; height: 26px; stroke: var(--accent); fill: none; stroke-width: 1.6; }\n    .zone b { font-size: .82rem; font-weight: 600; }\n    .zone small { font-size: .66rem; color: var(--muted); }\n\n    ul { list-style: none; margin: .7rem 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: .4rem; }\n    li {\n      display: grid; grid-template-columns: 26px 1fr auto; align-items: center; gap: .55rem;\n      padding: .45rem .55rem; background: var(--surface);\n      border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px;\n    }\n    .ext {\n      font-size: .52rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .03em; text-align: center;\n      padding: .25rem 0; border-radius: 4px;\n      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 22%, transparent); color: #cdbfff;\n    }\n    .meta { min-width: 0; }\n    .name { font-size: .7rem; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }\n    .size { font-size: .6rem; color: var(--muted); }\n    .bar { height: 3px; margin-top: .3rem; background: #202638; border-radius: 999px; overflow: hidden; }\n    .bar i { display: block; height: 100%; width: 0; background: var(--accent); transition: width .25s linear; }\n    li.done .bar i { background: var(--ok); }\n    .rm {\n      border: 0; background: none; color: var(--muted); cursor: pointer;\n      font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1; padding: .2rem .3rem; border-radius: 5px;\n    }\n    .rm:hover { color: var(--text); background: #ffffff12; }\n    .rm:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; }\n\n    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n      .zone, .bar i { transition: none; }\n      .zone.is-over { transform: none; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class=\"wrap\">\n    <label class=\"zone\" id=\"zone\">\n      <input class=\"sr\" type=\"file\" id=\"picker\" multiple />\n      <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n        <path d=\"M12 16V4m0 0L8 8m4-4 4 4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n        <path d=\"M3 15v3a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h14a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n      </svg>\n      <b>Drop files here</b>\n      <small>or click to browse · up to 10&nbsp;MB each</small>\n    </label>\n\n    <ul id=\"queue\" aria-live=\"polite\" aria-label=\"Selected files\"></ul>\n  </div>\n\n  <script>\n    var MAX_MB = 10;\n    var zone = document.getElementById(\"zone\");\n    var picker = document.getElementById(\"picker\");\n    var queue = document.getElementById(\"queue\");\n    var reduce = matchMedia(\"(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)\").matches;\n    var depth = 0;   // dragenter/dragleave fire per child; count instead of toggling\n\n    function human(bytes) {\n      if (bytes < 1024) return bytes + \" B\";\n      var kb = bytes / 1024;\n      if (kb < 1024) return kb.toFixed(0) + \" KB\";\n      return (kb / 1024).toFixed(1) + \" MB\";\n    }\n    function extOf(name) {\n      var i = name.lastIndexOf(\".\");\n      return (i > -1 ? name.slice(i + 1) : \"?\").slice(0, 4).toUpperCase();\n    }\n\n    function addRow(file) {\n      var li = document.createElement(\"li\");\n      var tooBig = file.size > MAX_MB * 1024 * 1024;\n\n      var ext = document.createElement(\"span\");\n      ext.className = \"ext\"; ext.textContent = extOf(file.name);\n\n      var meta = document.createElement(\"div\");\n      meta.className = \"meta\";\n      var name = document.createElement(\"div\");\n      name.className = \"name\"; name.textContent = file.name;\n      var size = document.createElement(\"div\");\n      size.className = \"size\";\n      // Say which file failed and why — never drop it silently.\n      size.textContent = tooBig ? human(file.size) + \" · too large, max \" + MAX_MB + \" MB\" : human(file.size);\n      if (tooBig) size.style.color = \"#f2555a\";\n      var bar = document.createElement(\"div\");\n      bar.className = \"bar\";\n      var fill = document.createElement(\"i\");\n      bar.appendChild(fill);\n      meta.appendChild(name); meta.appendChild(size);\n      if (!tooBig) meta.appendChild(bar);\n\n      var rm = document.createElement(\"button\");\n      rm.className = \"rm\"; rm.type = \"button\";\n      rm.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", \"Remove \" + file.name);\n      rm.textContent = \"×\";\n      rm.onclick = function () { li.remove(); };\n\n      li.appendChild(ext); li.appendChild(meta); li.appendChild(rm);\n      queue.appendChild(li);\n\n      // Stub progress. Replace with xhr.upload.onprogress for a real upload.\n      if (!tooBig) {\n        if (reduce) { fill.style.width = \"100%\"; li.classList.add(\"done\"); return; }\n        var pct = 0;\n        var timer = setInterval(function () {\n          pct = Math.min(pct + 8 + Math.random() * 14, 100);\n          fill.style.width = pct + \"%\";\n          if (pct >= 100) { clearInterval(timer); li.classList.add(\"done\"); }\n        }, 140);\n      }\n    }\n\n    function accept(list) {\n      for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) addRow(list[i]);\n    }\n\n    picker.addEventListener(\"change\", function () { accept(picker.files); picker.value = \"\"; });\n\n    // dragover must preventDefault or the drop event never fires.\n    zone.addEventListener(\"dragover\", function (e) { e.preventDefault(); });\n    zone.addEventListener(\"dragenter\", function (e) {\n      e.preventDefault(); depth++; zone.classList.add(\"is-over\");\n    });\n    zone.addEventListener(\"dragleave\", function () {\n      if (--depth <= 0) { depth = 0; zone.classList.remove(\"is-over\"); }\n    });\n    zone.addEventListener(\"drop\", function (e) {\n      e.preventDefault(); depth = 0; zone.classList.remove(\"is-over\");\n      // accept=\"\" filters the picker but NOT drops — validate here too.\n      if (e.dataTransfer && e.dataTransfer.files) accept(e.dataTransfer.files);\n    });\n\n    // Without this, a file dropped outside the zone navigates the page to it.\n    window.addEventListener(\"dragover\", function (e) { e.preventDefault(); });\n    window.addEventListener(\"drop\", function (e) { e.preventDefault(); });\n\n    // Seed the queue so the specimen shows its resting state.\n    [\n      { name: \"quarterly-report.pdf\", size: 2411724 },\n      { name: \"hero-banner@2x.png\", size: 845213 }\n    ].forEach(addRow);\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
}
